    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for August 5th is anchored by three high-upside plays that carry the load today. **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) is our strongest start, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Lowder; his 18% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s xERA makes him an elite option. He is closely followed by **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) and **Bryce Harper** (69.09), both of whom enjoy significant park and platoon advantages. **Aranda** in particular is surging, as the combination of a high-ceiling park and a soft matchup against Sugano propels him well into the elite tier of our daily projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation was leaving **Braden Montgomery** (46.78) on the bench. While he carries a decent projection, he failed to crack the top tier due to the stifling presence of Gray, whose ability to limit damage forced the optimizer to favor players with better matchup contexts. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jeremiah Jackson** (44.09), who carries a 36% rain risk at his venue. While he remains in the lineup, his status is the most volatile of our starters. Additionally, **Gavin Sheets** is currently slotted in with an assumed lineup position; should the official report move him down the order, his marginal efficiency score could drop below the threshold. \n\nWe are continuing to prioritize speed and situational alignment, which keeps **Justin Crawford** (57.47) in the mix despite a lower spot in the order. His role in our SB strategy remains critical, even with the modest projected efficiency. We\u2019ve successfully benched **Gleyber Torres** and **Jung Hoo Lee**, as their matchups against Woo and Bradford, respectively, rendered them sub-optimal compared to the current configuration of **Luis Arraez**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Daulton Varsho**. We head into the slate with a solid spread of production, provided the weather in **Jeremiah Jackson**\u2019s game holds up.",
